<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Returns policy</h1>
    <p>What can be returned, and the route a return has to take.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>The window</h2>
    <p>
      The shop's stated return window is <%= returnsWindowDays %> days from the day the item is transferred
      to you. Tell the shop inside that window if you intend to return something.
    </p>

    <h2>Firearms</h2>
    <div class="note note-pending">
      <h3>Return route pending publication</h3>
      <p>
        A firearm cannot simply be posted back. The lawful route for returning a transferred firearm depends
        on the dealer's licence and the jurisdiction, so the exact steps are supplied by the licence holder
        and published here after review. Contact the shop first and follow the instructions you are given.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Parts and accessories</h2>
    <p>
      Unused parts in their original packaging can normally be returned inside the window. Parts that have
      been fitted, modified or refinished cannot, because they can no longer be sold as new and their
      condition cannot be verified.
    </p>

    <h2>Faulty items</h2>
    <p>
      A manufacturing fault is handled under the manufacturer warranty and under your statutory rights,
      whichever gives you more. Tell the shop what happened, and do not attempt a repair first, because that
      normally voids the warranty.
    </p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      An accepted return is refunded by the method used to pay. Transfer fees already incurred by a third
      party licence holder are not refundable by this shop, because that money went to another business.
    </p>

    <h2>How to start a return</h2>
    <p>
      Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> with your order reference and a description of the problem.
      Do not send identity documents or licence numbers through the form.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
